  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\nA mid level trough will cross east through the Ohio Valley Thursday\nnight, bringing a few showers to areas north of the I-70 corridor.\nAfterwards, a closed low will track east through the lower Great\nLakes and bring in colder air aloft in its wake. \n\nA secondary frontal passage will also usher in a somewhat cooler \nairmass heading into the weekend. Daytime highs will only be in the \n50s Saturday and Sunday. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2)\nA dry forecast is expected after Friday through the end of the\nperiod. Starting Monday, temperatures will modify a little each day,\ngenerally in the low to mid 60s for highs and mid-upper 30s for lows.",
